# Angol-Elementos-Dados
Retrieve all 7 content markdown files from the Curso-de-Ingles project.

## When to Use
The user needs to read the content of the following markdown files from the project directory:
- `apostila-ingles-para-iniciantes-impresso.md`
- `Ingles-basico.md`
- `Ingles para Viagens.md`
- `frases-ingles-trabalho.md`
- `Ingles-Tecnico-Para-Informatica.md`
- `leia-e-escreva-melhor-em-ingles.md`
- `Dicionario-de-Siglas-e-Termos-Profissionais-em-Ingles.md`

## Procedure
1. Read all 7 markdown files simultaneously (they are independent)
2. Strip page marker placeholders (e.g., ` Page 1`, `• 1`, `\f`) from each file
3. Return clean content for each file

## Pitfalls
- `ls` command does not work in the terminal environment (throws `SyntaxError: invalid syntax`) — use Python `os.listdir` instead
- File paths must use forward slashes and the exact path: `.../Curso-de-Ingles/Ingles/output/`

## Verification
Each file should read as plain text with no page marker artifacts.
